Deploying Desktop Backgrounds with group policies:
1.configure storage locationns for background image
  1.shared folder -> create a folder inside the c drive with read only permission for all users, copy the image to this shared folder
  2.now select folder -> right click on it and go to properties
  3.go to sharing -> Advanced sharing
  4.check 'share this folder' -> permissions -> clck on add-> search for 'domain users' -> click on ok
  5.permission for domain users is read only
  6. note down the network path of folder
  7.make sure path is accesible on client machine (win +R) and search the path

2.Create and configure GPO for desktop wallpaper
 1.win +R and type : gpmc.msc
 2.right click on the domain and select "create a GPO in this domain and lik it there" and named it 'background-image' 
 3. right click on this policy and select edit to open the group policy management editor
 4.navigate to  "policy template" go to users configuration -> policies -> Administrative templates -> desktop ->desktop ->desktop wallpaper
 5.double click desktop wallpaper -> select enabled -> enter the unc path to image -> select fit or any other option for wallpaper style
 6.click "apply and ok" then run "gpupdate /force" im cmd to update settings

